# ---- allowlist: only competition code is pushed ------------------------------
# Participation is individual and confidential; competition data, anything derived
# from it, notes, logs and learning material must never reach a remote. Rather than
# listing everything to exclude, ignore everything and re-include code explicitly.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!.python-version
!*.py
!*.ipynb
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock

# ---- exceptions to the allowlist (later rules win) ---------------------------
# the "Three Tasks, Seven Days" course (day1-day7, playbook, quizzes) — private
course/

# environments and build output — these contain .py files
.venv/
__pycache__/
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
kout/

# organizer-provided starter notebooks
*/starter-notebook*.ipynb

# embeds SHORTLIST_B64, a candidate shortlist computed from the competition images
kaggle-loftr-verify.ipynb
# embeds CAND, 3,439 indices of competition images selected for extra orientations
kaggle-rot-canonical.ipynb
# PICKS: hand-audited test answers keyed by question ID (the v8 re-selection table)
pitcher/pitcher-solution-v8.ipynb
